     1	# Movement brief — MOVEMENT-007 · "The Long Stair"
     2	
     3	- Book id: the-fractured-path / book-07-void-roads (Monroe Jackson 1.3 edition)
     4	- Author: Opus (Claude Opus 5.5) requested
     5	- Chapters: 45–52 → `manuscript/chapter-45.md` … `chapter-52.md`
     6	- Word budget: 40,000
     7	- Days: 111–115 past the Line
     8	- Owner names: canon only. The miller, Millrace's ford-keeper and patients, the six on the rim, the second Anchor specialist, the hide-woman, the crew of three and Teague's crew stay unnamed. **No faces on the rim.**
     9	- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; twelve years carrying the case for people he cannot see [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6]; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
    10	- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈40 per 10k. ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for all six, plus Pike and Teague.
    11	
    12	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — "Six years I've wanted a face" and OWNER-pending #50 (#50 default in force), binding.]** Seln's protected council line stays WORD FOR WORD: "…People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face." Edition canon is that he has carried the case TWELVE years (fifteen in service). Until the owner rules, do not gloss the six, do not invent an event six years back, and do not state the case's twelve years in the same scene or have anyone do the arithmetic. Elsewhere in the movement the case is a twelve-year matter, as the packet now says. (The page already has Seln dating the registry's survey of the circles at "five years ago by the stake, maybe six" in ch34; you may leave that echo to the reader, but do not point at it.) Write so that changing the one numeral later would need no other change.
    13	
    14	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
    15	
    16	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — Oryn's circuit and Millrace (EXC-B7-003, owner-resolved 2026-09-04; do not reopen), binding.]** Oryn left Thornwater by the northern wicket at first light on the 111th saying, in the protected words, "North in the morning… I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board… Thornwater's on my route." Millrace is one day SOUTH of Lowmarch on the Stair road, and she is at her table there on the 113th. The owner's ruling is that both stand: her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days (the track from the northern wicket bends west and then south, as ch44 shows). Do not contradict either. Let it be true on the page in one plain line when the five find her at Millrace (for example which stop she cut or sent word to, as the packet's "word sent up the route" already allows); do not have anyone remark that she said north.
    17	
    18	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — inheritance from Movement 6's surviving prose (Sol plan audit §8), binding.]** Read the edition's own closed chapters from disk and STATE_LEDGER "AFTER MOVEMENT 6" before drafting. The audit's list follows.
    19	>
    20	> Movement 7’s packet already carries the day-111 start, Oryn gone, mule with the crew, Lira two weeks into the order, and the report west (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20`). It must additionally inherit:
    21	>
    22	> - **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
    23	> - **Bodies:** Lira’s left arm remains slung and may hold nothing until first snow, although all eight marks have taken; right tibia may run; right ankle remains taped/unmended and her left arm cannot span the bow. Brom’s hand is whole. Karis’s voice is whole but she must not lecture for a week. Cael’s calf is closed and forearm yellow-marked. Seln is unhurt (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121,129–201`; `chapter-43.md:125–159`).
    24	> - **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
    25	> - **Knowledge:** all six know Cael functioned inside the Ring and know that his self-reading found something, but none except Cael knows what; Oryn knows the mechanism but not that Seln supplied Shadow; Karis’s hypothesis is neither spoken nor entered; the Quieting name and five findings are shared; nobody has put a verb between the facts (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–105,113–117`).
    26	> - **Research state:** Karis’s kinds-count is covered and unsaid; finding four says only “five or six”; stake thirty-two remains Lira’s guess; the four wheres include two map rings marked *guess* and Seln’s unplaced childhood round (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:125–159`; `chapter-43.md:3–53`; `chapter-44.md:71–95`).
    27	> - **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
    28	> - **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
    29	
    30	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator O3]
    31	
    32	**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-17.md`, `chapter-18.md`, `chapter-19.md`, `chapter-20.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §7 (Shadow twice; Anchor unbinding), §8 (Stair allowance), §10 (Ch17–20), §11 (faceless; the rim sees only the outside), §12 C3; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 6 append); `v3-runs/book-07/CONFLICT-B7-CH18.md` (why Millrace).
    33	
    34	## Where we enter
    35	
    36	First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
    37	
    38	## What this movement is for
    39	
    40	A trap priced to fit, read before it is sprung; the sixth chair filled on her own terms of service; a floor built to disarm six people that disarms five; and the first registry object the crew has ever owned, with a word in it that is a direction. Turns and promises:
    41	
    42	- **Thornwater → Lowmarch (111–112), the first cold.** The fourth honest catalogue from the rise.
    43	- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
    44	- **The second slip** on the nail of read-and-returned (protected text). Pike, unasked: "Nothing else ever… I'd not take it." Karis: "That's the carter's second circle." **Seln's anatomy** (protected lines): registry prose; the same clerk; a size, not a wage; a floor he *knows*; "pre-restriction inventory"; "The boy's the price of the case."
    45	- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** [OWNER-pending #50] Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
    46	- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
    47	- **The reading taught on the road:** "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes…" Surface at ten: Tide *there*, the first thing that has ever been there at ten. A minute of the long one: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things. "You're built to arrive." / "Yes… That's what I am." "He asked twice and got one." / "That's the rate."
    48	- **The Stair from the ridge at dusk:** a bowl wider and shallower than the Ring's; a bare floor with no ring; a square hole with three lit steps and then dark. The line at forty paces ("Two hundred. I'll pace it in the morning."). **Two stakes numbered thirty-two**, one under five cold terms of scale [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] and one under one or two, with the **stroke and the bar**: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed." Camp at the line.
    49	- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty-five yards** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Once Cael is within ten feet of the knot, Anchor perception finds it; he then makes the separate purposeful unbinding, without assigning that action a measured reach, rate or price [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
    50	- **Out at dark:** "There. Back… The clock started again." The bolt-head cut and the shaft drawn; an hour on Brom; a quarter on Lira ("It held a stair…"). His bill: the suite spent on a week's rest. **Seln breaks a stock across the stone**: "No faces." The log (protected). **Teague's crew at full dark** (protected exchange); he does not ask how.
    51	- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
    52	
    53	## What must remain true / withheld
    54	
    55	- **Shadow is used once in this movement**, unseen and never attributable. That is its second and last use in the book.
    56	- **The rim saw a practitioner walk out declaring, and saw nothing work inside.** Teague saw the same and asks nothing.
    57	- Faceless: no seals, no names, no office. The specialist is not the Ostrand-road woman: the same craft, a different weight in the laying.
    58	- The case is untouched. The index and the stroke-and-bar are not decoded. Nobody theorizes.
    59	- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
    60	- Teague's crew is unnamed, including in Teague's window. The healer of no Path does not appear until M8.
    61	
    62	## What the author owns
    63	
    64	The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
    65	
    66	## Where we leave pressure
    67	
    68	Day 115, at the stone in full sun. The kit is on Brom's good shoulder and his bad one is mended once. Lira's arm is closed again with the sling higher. The ledger is in Seln's coat; twenty-nine sheets and forty-one kinds. A brass edge lies on a map. A dead man's last word was *bearing*. "We're going to go look."
