    55	"Five years," Seln said. He had come to it as he came to everything, along the wall, reading the ground, and he stood over the open book with his hands at his sides. "By the scale on the case. By the stakes. He was working. He stopped in the middle of a word and put the pen down and left the book open and the cord out and the case's lid on the floor, and he went up forty steps, and he didn't come back for any of it." He did not kneel. "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another."
    56	
