    90	
    91	Lira gave sheets. She did it one-handed, off the middle box's stack, the arm across her chest and the taped foot flat on the fused floor, and she did it before Karis said "Sheet" nearly every time, because she had watched the charcoal reach a sheet's edge twenty-eight times and had learned the length of a wall's course as she had learned the length of a floor: by standing on it. Brom refilled the lamps. Seln read. Oryn watched. Cael catalogued the four of them doing the four things, and found that it was a unit at work with no Path in any of them and nothing to fight, and that it looked exactly like a unit at work.
