   193	He laid the two pieces on the turf, side by side, and went and sat down by the mules.
   194	
   195	Cael opened Hesk's book on his knee. Lira had put it into his lap when she came over the stone, with the strap done up, and had said nothing; and he held the pencil in his bandaged left hand, since the right would not close.
   196	
   197	*Hundred and fourteenth day, night. Outside the stone. All six out. Brom: a bolt through the right shoulder, drawn and mended, an hour. Lira: the arm opened on the stair wall and is shut again, a quarter. Thirteen bolts loosed at us in the day, and one hit. Ours: five, and none shot.*
   198	
   199	He ruled a line, and put down what he had spent, one thing to a line, as he had on the Fallow.
   200	
   201	*Anchor: looking, at the two bars, first light. I saw the fence go up. I stood two counts to see it, and Brom had those two counts with a bolt in him.*
   202	
   203	*Shadow: once, from the fourth step to the old bar. Lira saw it go, from below. Seln turned his back. Three were round the door. The six were two hundred and sixty yards off, with a lip between; not one had a line to me. Let go in the rut. It holds. Dead to the elbows; I had to watch my own hand.*
   204	
