+# Movement 007 source-distance tracking
+
+Independent side-by-side read of source chapters 17–20 against manuscript chapters 45–52. Protected units, wording quoted in `MOVEMENT-007.md`, and facts or event sequences required by the packet, `BOOK_MAP.md`, `STATE_LEDGER.md`, or the author's pre-prose `EVENT-LIST.md` were excluded wherever the manuscript supplied a genuinely new telling.
+
+The requested pair-output probe was run. Its movement total (3% skeleton / 17% close) is not a count of genuine tracking. The only probe scene over its automatic 15% skeleton threshold is chapter 46 scene 3, whose strong pairs are the protected Seln and Cael council lines. The other displayed exact pairs are likewise protected dialogue, notices, or log entries; the lower-scoring pairs are common-language accidents. The findings below are unprotected sentence-content and beat-order matches that survive those exclusions.
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Three genuine tracked passages.** Chapter 52 scene 2 is densely tracked, with two passages in the same short scene. Chapter 52 scene 3 contains one isolated passage. Every scene in chapters 45–51, and every other scene in chapter 52, contains none.
+
